Sound-chip and FM synthesizer cores (vendored)

Source:  each core's own, named below. Some come by way of
         https://github.com/kyorohiro/tetorica-soundchip-native, commit
         b4f2543c08f3a6b2c780d723263dee444ff13343 (b4f2543, 2026-11-16), which collects cores
         from their upstreams and records where each came from.
Licence: each core keeps its own. LICENSE is the Apache License 2.0 (the text of
         vendor/msfa/COPYING), which also covers what was written for Pro Wave here.

vendor/msfa: the six-operator FM core of music-synthesizer-for-android
  Upstream: https://github.com/google/music-synthesizer-for-android, commit
            f67d41d313b7dc85f6fb99e79e515cc9d208cfff (app/src/main/jni), Copyright 2012-2013
            Google Inc., Apache License 2.0 (vendor/msfa/COPYING; every source file carries
            the Apache header).
  As vendored by Tetorica, with its changes (marked "Tetorica" in the files, Apache-2.0,
  described in vendor/msfa/UPSTREAM.md): live operator level, frequency and feedback
  control in env.{h,cc} and dx7note.{h,cc}, bounds for extreme frequencies in freqlut.cc
  and fm_core.cc, a self-contained aligned_buf.h, and a switch for the scalar path in
  synth.h. These files are unchanged from Tetorica's copy.
  Here: aligned_buf.h, controllers.h, dx7note, env, exp2, fm_core, fm_op_kernel, freqlut,
  lfo, patch, pitchenv, sin (.h and .cc each), synth.h, COPYING, UPSTREAM.md and
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
  Not here: synth_unit, resofilter, ringbuffer and module.h (Pro Wave allocates the voices
  itself, and so does not carry the electric-piano voice that synth_unit.cc starts with), and
  everything else of both repositories. No voice or voice bank of any instrument is here.

vendor/ymfm: Yamaha FM sound-chip cores
  Upstream: https://github.com/aaronsgiles/ymfm, commit
            81aec25ccbb98f4873a255f7551ac4dadac59b4a (81aec25, 2026-07-27), src/, Copyright (c)
            2021 Aaron Giles, BSD-3-Clause (vendor/ymfm/LICENSE; every file carries the
            notice). Taken from ymfm itself and unchanged: Tetorica's copy of it carries
            changes and names no upstream commit.
  Here: ymfm.h, ymfm_fm.h, ymfm_fm.ipp, and ymfm_opl, ymfm_opn, ymfm_ssg, ymfm_adpcm and
  ymfm_pcm (.h and .cpp each): the OPL and OPN families and what their files include.
  Not here: the OPM, OPQ, OPZ and OPX families, ymfm_misc and the examples.

